
# Button — headless. Ported from shadcn/radix (tmp/study). Renders a native <button> carrying the stable theming hooks
# (data-slot / data-variant / data-size) plus a pass-through class, an optional disabled flag, and a children slot. No
# baked styling: a theme targets [data-slot=button] (and the data-variant / data-size facets) or passes classes via the
# `class` prop. The click handler is passed in via `press`. This is the Radix/Ark headless model, not shadcn's styled
# one — the parts + state attributes are here; the look is entirely the consumer's.

load @term/site/code/view/render
  find element
  find text
load @term/site/code/dom/dom
  find view
  find append

view button
  take host, like view
  take class
  take variant
  take size
  # `node button` forces the element: inside a component named `button`, `view button` is the component again. It was
  # written `view tag-button`, which no lowering reads, so it rendered a `<tag-button>` element (found 2026-10-02)
  node button
    seed data-slot, text <button>
    seed data-variant, read variant
    seed data-size, read size
    seed class, read class
    slot
